WEBVTT

00:05.672 --> 00:09.092
[thunder rumbling]

00:09.092 --> 00:11.469
[loud thunderclap crashing]

00:13.346 --> 00:15.140
[Oz] I ever tell you
about Rex Calabrese?

00:15.807 --> 00:17.017
[Victor] Uh, no.

00:20.979 --> 00:22.522
He ran my neighborhood
when I was a kid.

00:22.647 --> 00:24.232
[distant siren wailing]

00:24.232 --> 00:27.027
Had this, uh, gold Cadillac
with white leather seats.

00:27.027 --> 00:29.112
- [fire roars]
- [Oz chuckles]

00:29.112 --> 00:30.196
Beautiful.

00:31.114 --> 00:32.532
When it rolled down your street,

00:32.657 --> 00:34.659
I mean, it felt like your block
was blessed.

00:35.869 --> 00:38.663
Rex's ride,
it wasn't just a car,

00:38.788 --> 00:40.582
it was a fuckin' chariot.

00:41.541 --> 00:44.252
Made a kid with a bum leg
feel like even he could be king.

00:44.252 --> 00:45.378
[chuckles]

00:48.548 --> 00:50.383
- The end of an era.
- [thunder crashing]

00:50.383 --> 00:52.469
[rain pattering]

00:52.469 --> 00:53.511
[Oz] Come on.

00:53.636 --> 00:55.722
[Victor] Uh, what about Sofia?

00:55.847 --> 00:57.265
- Now that she knows--
- Sofia?

00:57.265 --> 00:59.684
Ah, chick's a thorn
without a prick, kid.

00:59.809 --> 01:01.478
We get our shrooms back,
she won't matter.

01:01.478 --> 01:02.729
Right.

01:04.356 --> 01:05.857
- Sorry, Oz.
- For what?

01:06.399 --> 01:07.734
For wrecking your chariot.

01:09.027 --> 01:10.445
I only got one shot at this.

01:11.237 --> 01:14.282
You know, I-I see that now.

01:14.282 --> 01:15.909
You came back, Vic.

01:17.035 --> 01:18.620
Put your ass on the line for me.

01:19.496 --> 01:21.289
A hundred Maseratis
couldn't replace that.

01:21.289 --> 01:23.541
Though this one came
pretty damn close.

01:24.501 --> 01:26.628
It's you and me now, kid.
Till the end.

01:26.628 --> 01:29.714
Ain't it time we get ourselves
some goddamn respect?

01:29.839 --> 01:31.049
Huh?

01:31.174 --> 01:32.884
- Let's fucking go.
- [laughs]

01:33.009 --> 01:34.052
- I like that.
- [chuckles]

01:34.177 --> 01:36.429
Alright. Here's our ride.
[whistles]

01:38.181 --> 01:39.474
[car horn honks]

01:45.271 --> 01:46.648
[Oz] Welcome to the party,
fellas!

01:46.648 --> 01:47.816
Oz, your fuckin' car.

01:47.816 --> 01:49.275
Ah, what are you gonna do?

01:49.275 --> 01:50.944
Only the good die young.

01:51.069 --> 01:53.363
So, listen. When I eat, you eat.

01:53.863 --> 01:54.948
How it's always been, right?

01:54.948 --> 01:56.366
- Yeah, 'course.
- Alright, good.

01:56.366 --> 01:57.992
Well I got somethin'
beautiful going.

01:57.992 --> 01:59.869
A new drug. Homegrown.

01:59.869 --> 02:01.538
I was gonna cut you in on it,

02:01.538 --> 02:03.832
but fuckin' Maronis took it
off my plate before I could.

02:03.832 --> 02:04.916
So, how we getting it back?

02:05.041 --> 02:06.918
- [explosion booming]
- Whoa.

02:07.043 --> 02:08.420
[Oz] Hey, listen.

02:08.545 --> 02:10.422
The Maronis got a huge
fuckin' blind spot

02:10.547 --> 02:12.090
just beggin' to be exploited.

02:12.215 --> 02:13.925
Come here, look at this.

02:15.468 --> 02:16.845
Yo, what up, fam.

02:16.845 --> 02:18.430
I'm getting a slick new
back piece

02:18.555 --> 02:19.806
from the Chicano
legend himself--

02:19.806 --> 02:21.099
- [Oz] Taj Maroni.
- [laughter]

02:21.224 --> 02:22.642
This is the heir to
Sal's throne.

02:22.767 --> 02:25.228
...to tell all you
motherfuckers the Maronis

02:25.228 --> 02:27.480
are about to take back
what was taken from us.

02:27.480 --> 02:29.941
This stupid motherfucker,
he's just beggin' to be got.

02:30.066 --> 02:32.110
["Note Siah" by Farshad playing]

02:36.948 --> 02:39.325
[muffled gunfire]

02:43.580 --> 02:44.706
- [splattering]
- [body thuds]

02:44.706 --> 02:45.790
- [music stops]
- [Oz] Hey!

02:45.915 --> 02:47.542
[Taj] Yo, what the fuck?

02:47.542 --> 02:49.210
- Mikey!
- [Mikey] I got him!

02:49.210 --> 02:50.920
[dramatic, frenetic music
playing]

02:50.920 --> 02:52.464
[Mikey] Don't you fuckin'--

02:53.423 --> 02:54.299
[Victor] Stop!

02:55.967 --> 02:56.968
[Taj grunts]

03:00.513 --> 03:01.973
[Taj grunts]

03:04.684 --> 03:05.727
Hey. Hey.

03:05.727 --> 03:07.979
Hold still, you piece of shit.

03:08.104 --> 03:09.564
Oh, you are so fucked, man.

03:09.564 --> 03:12.025
You messed with the wrong
fuckin' family!

03:12.150 --> 03:15.195
My-My mother, my father,
they won't stand for this--

03:17.155 --> 03:18.490
That's what I'm countin' on.

03:19.032 --> 03:20.784
[ominous music playing]

03:20.784 --> 03:22.035
[cell doors whir, clang]

03:26.122 --> 03:27.499
[distant buzzer sounds]

03:29.125 --> 03:30.543
[distant indistinct chatter]

03:30.543 --> 03:32.212
[music fades]

03:36.841 --> 03:38.218
[distant buzzer sounds]

03:40.845 --> 03:41.846
What do you want?

03:41.971 --> 03:43.181
I want what's mine.

03:44.557 --> 03:46.309
What your wife stole from me.

03:46.309 --> 03:48.269
I want my fuckin' shrooms.

03:48.269 --> 03:51.314
Our son is not a pawn.

03:51.314 --> 03:52.899
There is a code.

03:53.024 --> 03:54.109
Oh, is that right?

03:54.109 --> 03:55.610
What, I take the wrong
Maroni? That it?

03:55.610 --> 03:57.487
[bangs table] You do not
threaten my family.

03:57.487 --> 03:58.947
Jesus, Sal.

03:58.947 --> 04:00.115
Put your dick away.

04:00.824 --> 04:02.242
Don't forget who I got at home.

04:04.035 --> 04:05.370
[Salvatore grumbles]

04:13.211 --> 04:16.631
We meet early, before sunrise,
for the exchange.

04:16.631 --> 04:18.466
Make sure my shrooms
are ready to go.

04:19.843 --> 04:21.845
And what do you say we keep it
nice and intimate?

04:21.845 --> 04:23.221
Just you, me, and Taj.

04:23.346 --> 04:25.515
No. My wife doesn't go alone.

04:25.515 --> 04:28.476
Fine. I'll let you take
one guard, Nadia.

04:28.935 --> 04:30.729
- 'Cause I'm a gentleman.
- [scoffs]

04:32.355 --> 04:33.148
Sal.

04:33.148 --> 04:34.816
[in Farsi]

04:40.572 --> 04:41.865
Hey!

04:43.700 --> 04:46.828
Honor your end,
and Taj will be just fine.

04:49.789 --> 04:50.915
Now...

04:51.750 --> 04:52.917
we got a deal or what?

04:53.043 --> 04:54.586
- [buzzer sounds]
- [lock clicks]

04:54.711 --> 04:56.087
[man over PA]
All security officers

04:56.212 --> 04:58.590
report to administration
before the end of shift.

04:58.715 --> 05:00.967
[door squeaks, clangs shut]

05:02.135 --> 05:03.803
- [buzzer sounds]
- [lock clangs]

05:06.890 --> 05:08.475
- [door clangs]
- [lock clicks]

05:10.101 --> 05:11.436
Eleven o'clock.

05:11.561 --> 05:12.771
Red jacket.

05:15.231 --> 05:16.524
[newscaster on TV]
Breaking news.

05:16.524 --> 05:18.777
A tragedy at the home
of late mob boss

05:18.902 --> 05:21.071
- Carmine Falcone...
- Hey, come on!

05:21.071 --> 05:22.572
Some of us got places to be.

05:22.572 --> 05:24.783
...Sofia Falcone,
Carmine's daughter,

05:24.908 --> 05:28.286
is currently one of the only
confirmed survivors.

05:28.411 --> 05:30.789
GCPD has yet to release
any results

05:30.914 --> 05:32.999
of their still-early
investigation,

05:33.124 --> 05:36.670
but these deaths follow
a period of intense violence

05:36.670 --> 05:39.798
between the Falcone and
the Maroni crime families.

05:39.923 --> 05:42.384
[dramatic, uneasy music playing]

05:45.136 --> 05:46.971
[indistinct radio chatter]

05:51.851 --> 05:53.978
[music darkens]

06:04.364 --> 06:05.573
[man] Ms. Falcone?

06:08.326 --> 06:09.911
Please, I prefer Sofia.

06:10.495 --> 06:11.579
Police Chief Bock.

06:12.205 --> 06:13.873
Gotham City Police Department.

06:13.998 --> 06:14.958
[reporters] Ms. Falcone!

06:14.958 --> 06:16.501
[reporters clamoring]

06:16.626 --> 06:17.669
Can we, um...?

06:19.295 --> 06:20.171
Yeah.

06:20.296 --> 06:22.340
[helicopter whirring overhead]

06:24.217 --> 06:26.928
You said you remained
in the greenhouse all night.

06:27.721 --> 06:30.348
Gia and I, yes.
There was an argument

06:30.473 --> 06:32.684
between my Uncle Luca
and my cousin Johnny.

06:33.351 --> 06:35.603
Carla asked me
to take Gia outside...

06:37.147 --> 06:38.398
keep her away from it.

06:38.982 --> 06:40.400
[Bock] What was the argument
about?

06:40.984 --> 06:42.736
[vehicle drives off]

06:43.403 --> 06:45.697
I, uh, only heard
bits and pieces.

06:45.822 --> 06:48.450
Something about Luca's wife,
Tina.

06:50.035 --> 06:55.248
There were rumors
about an affair, but I, uh...

06:56.875 --> 06:59.461
It wasn't a good situation
for a young girl to be in.

06:59.461 --> 07:01.880
Johnny Viti's
not among the dead.

07:03.089 --> 07:05.050
Any idea where
we might find him?

07:06.217 --> 07:07.427
I'm sorry, no.

07:09.554 --> 07:12.057
He must've left last night.

07:13.224 --> 07:15.643
I didn't come back inside
until this morning.

07:16.895 --> 07:18.229
And that's when I, uh...

07:19.731 --> 07:20.982
[whispers] ...saw the bodies.

07:21.691 --> 07:22.901
Excuse me.

07:23.860 --> 07:25.945
Awfully suspicious,
don't you think?

07:27.197 --> 07:30.617
Prominent crime family in Gotham
wiped out by a gas leak?

07:30.742 --> 07:33.244
[uneasy music playing]

07:36.873 --> 07:39.334
Is that a question
you'd like me to answer?

07:41.419 --> 07:42.295
Tell me,

07:43.046 --> 07:44.631
is it common for
the chief of police

07:44.756 --> 07:46.925
to respond to house calls?

07:47.926 --> 07:49.678
We are quite a ways
from the city.

07:49.678 --> 07:52.013
I hope you didn't come
to my home

07:52.013 --> 07:54.683
to throw my family's death
in my face.

07:54.683 --> 07:56.935
It's a new era in Gotham,
Ms. Falcone.

07:57.060 --> 07:58.520
The mayor-elect's got a mandate

07:58.520 --> 08:00.563
to put an end
to the scum of this city.

08:00.563 --> 08:03.191
So you're here to see it
for yourself.

08:04.442 --> 08:05.443
Hmm?

08:07.445 --> 08:10.198
And I suppose you and your boys
are gonna go for beers later?

08:11.074 --> 08:12.283
To celebrate?

08:13.243 --> 08:16.121
Maybe swap photos
of my dead relatives?

08:17.455 --> 08:19.791
Or are you going to sell those
to the Gazette

08:20.458 --> 08:22.961
to make up for all
the lost kickbacks?

08:27.465 --> 08:29.050
We're doing our due diligence.

08:30.677 --> 08:32.846
If you hear from Johnny Viti,
give us a call.

08:34.305 --> 08:35.640
Sorry for your loss.

08:40.687 --> 08:42.981
[bird calling]

08:43.106 --> 08:45.108
[liquid sloshing]

08:45.817 --> 08:47.986
- [door opens]
- [Viti breathing shakily]

08:48.111 --> 08:49.362
[door closes]

08:49.487 --> 08:52.115
- [footsteps approaching]
- [keys jingling]

08:52.115 --> 08:54.242
[grunting]

08:54.784 --> 08:56.578
[Sofia] The cops are
looking for you, Johnny.

08:58.705 --> 09:01.708
Although I get the sense they'd
rather find you dead than alive.

09:03.543 --> 09:04.836
[panting]

09:05.378 --> 09:06.588
You're not looking too good.

09:07.339 --> 09:08.256
[groans]

09:08.256 --> 09:10.008
[breathing rapidly]

09:13.845 --> 09:15.597
[pained grunts]

09:18.308 --> 09:19.684
The fuck is wrong with you?

09:21.061 --> 09:22.437
You're fucking sick.

09:23.021 --> 09:25.398
What kind of person kills
their own fuckin' family?

09:26.733 --> 09:29.611
- I need untraceable cash.
- [sighs]

09:29.611 --> 09:32.781
I know that my father would have
kept it somewhere close.

09:33.406 --> 09:36.117
And all you gotta do is show me.

09:36.117 --> 09:38.119
- And then I'll let you go.
- Right.

09:38.119 --> 09:39.371
[chuckles]

09:40.038 --> 09:41.623
You think I'm a fuckin' idiot?

09:42.874 --> 09:44.334
The second I do what you want,

09:44.334 --> 09:45.752
you fucking kill me.

09:47.879 --> 09:49.798
So just fuckin' do it already.

09:50.340 --> 09:52.092
Oh, please, Johnny.

09:53.885 --> 09:55.303
You're not that brave.

09:56.846 --> 10:00.058
But if you need more time
to think, you got it.

10:00.183 --> 10:02.310
[chains rattling]

10:03.019 --> 10:05.480
Although you should know,
it gets very cold down here.

10:06.189 --> 10:08.233
And with the work that it takes
your body

10:08.900 --> 10:11.486
to keep your organs alive...

10:12.237 --> 10:13.780
[ominous music playing]

10:13.905 --> 10:14.948
...you won't last long.

10:15.073 --> 10:16.408
Wait!

10:16.533 --> 10:18.493
[screams]

10:18.493 --> 10:20.704
[newscaster] Several members
of the Falcone family

10:20.704 --> 10:22.997
are still reported missing,
including Johnny Viti...

10:22.997 --> 10:24.958
[Eve] She knows you
killed her brother,

10:25.083 --> 10:26.668
and now she's gassed
her entire family.

10:26.668 --> 10:27.752
[Oz] Doll, let's relax.

10:27.877 --> 10:30.130
[Eve] Don't tell me to relax.

10:30.255 --> 10:31.756
I was your alibi, Oz.

10:31.881 --> 10:32.966
You made me that.

10:33.091 --> 10:34.718
Keep your voice down, alright?

10:34.718 --> 10:36.511
The guys don't know
all the details.

10:36.511 --> 10:38.638
You got too many plates
spinning.

10:38.763 --> 10:40.765
Listen, sweetheart, I know
you can't see it right now,

10:40.890 --> 10:42.934
but all this shit goin' down,
it's a good thing.

10:43.476 --> 10:46.187
I put it all in motion.
Luca, the Family...

10:46.187 --> 10:48.106
Sofia just took the bait,
that's all.

10:48.565 --> 10:50.775
Baby, do you even know when
you're full of shit anymore?

10:50.900 --> 10:52.652
- Huh?
- Me and the girls.

10:52.777 --> 10:54.529
You dangled us in front of her.

10:54.529 --> 10:57.198
- I didn't dangle you.
- You think it's a good thing?

10:57.198 --> 11:00.702
The Hangman knowing
their names, their faces...

11:01.411 --> 11:03.121
She's gunning for us now.

11:03.997 --> 11:06.082
While Taj Maroni sits
in my apartment.

11:06.082 --> 11:08.251
[Oz] The fuck
was I supposed to do?

11:08.251 --> 11:09.794
They stole my shit.

11:09.919 --> 11:11.046
Come on, doll.

11:11.046 --> 11:12.630
Nothing's gonna happen to you.

11:12.756 --> 11:14.632
Nothing's gonna happen to you.
I won't let it.

11:15.258 --> 11:17.969
All I'm askin' is for you to
hang tight just a little longer.

11:18.094 --> 11:18.970
That's it.

11:19.804 --> 11:22.474
And then it's you and me
on top of the world, baby.

11:22.599 --> 11:24.225
I need you to fix this.

11:24.225 --> 11:26.102
That's what I do. I fix things.

11:26.102 --> 11:28.188
Don't I fix things? Huh?

11:28.188 --> 11:31.524
[newscaster] ...there is no
threat to rescue workers...

11:31.649 --> 11:33.068
That's all I ever fuckin' do.

11:37.072 --> 11:39.324
[newscaster] As of now,
GCPD has yet to confirm

11:39.449 --> 11:42.243
- the total deceased...
- Members of Falcone family dead.

11:42.243 --> 11:44.079
Boo-hoo-hoo. Turn that shit off.

11:45.497 --> 11:46.706
Jesus fucking Christ.

11:47.791 --> 11:48.583
Look.

11:48.583 --> 11:50.460
I know this shit's grim,

11:50.460 --> 11:52.837
but none of those fucks
were friends of ours.

11:53.463 --> 11:54.673
They never made us.

11:55.799 --> 11:58.343
Luca Falcone didn't even know
your fuckin' names.

12:00.178 --> 12:01.805
So who ya missing?

12:01.805 --> 12:04.057
That skinny little pussy,
Johnny Viti?

12:04.974 --> 12:05.850
Milos?

12:06.810 --> 12:08.603
Guy wore lifts in his shoes.
We all knew it.

12:09.896 --> 12:11.439
The way I see it,

12:11.439 --> 12:13.108
Sofia done us a favor.

12:14.150 --> 12:17.404
- One family down, one to go.
- [men chuckling]

12:17.404 --> 12:19.948
Now, let's get back what
belongs to us, alright?

12:19.948 --> 12:21.449
- [man 1] All right.
- Get the fuck out.

12:21.449 --> 12:23.326
- [man 2] Let's go, brother.
- [Oz] Let's do it.

12:23.326 --> 12:24.536
Hey, come on.

12:25.537 --> 12:26.705
You. Come here.

12:27.997 --> 12:28.873
[man 1] Come on.

12:28.998 --> 12:30.333
I'm gonna need you with my ma.

12:30.333 --> 12:33.753
- Oz, I thought I'd, uh...
- [door closes]

12:33.878 --> 12:35.296
...be with you and the guys.

12:35.922 --> 12:37.173
I'm ready, I swear--

12:37.173 --> 12:38.717
I know you wanna get
in the fight, kid,

12:38.842 --> 12:40.885
but I ain't got no one else
I can trust, and look.

12:41.011 --> 12:43.304
Sofia's gonna come for us.
Whether it's today or tomorrow,

12:43.304 --> 12:46.141
she's gonna do whatever the fuck
it takes, and I can't have--

12:46.141 --> 12:49.394
I mean, my ma, she's,
you know...

12:50.270 --> 12:51.813
She's what keeps me good.

12:52.772 --> 12:54.107
I gotta know she's alright.

12:54.232 --> 12:55.400
Yeah. Done.

12:55.525 --> 12:58.737
I'm gonna...
I'll-I'll take care of her.

12:59.446 --> 13:00.321
I promise.

13:02.741 --> 13:04.367
[Bruno] Hold still,
stop squirming.

13:04.367 --> 13:06.119
- Get him up.
- [Taj grunting]

13:06.244 --> 13:07.996
[tense music playing]

13:11.624 --> 13:12.959
Let's get you home.

13:18.631 --> 13:19.799
[door opens]

13:22.594 --> 13:23.386
[music fades]

13:23.386 --> 13:25.555
[Viti shivering]

13:25.555 --> 13:27.098
[exhales]

13:30.101 --> 13:31.644
How you doing, Johnny?

13:31.770 --> 13:33.646
[sinister music playing]

13:33.646 --> 13:36.024
You ready to head back
to the house?

13:36.900 --> 13:40.195
Maybe warm yourself
by a nice fire,

13:40.945 --> 13:43.073
light an expensive cigar?

13:43.073 --> 13:44.949
[Viti coughing]

13:47.619 --> 13:48.620
Or...

13:49.996 --> 13:52.123
do you want to die
down here in the dark,

13:52.248 --> 13:53.625
with all the greats?

13:56.169 --> 13:57.545
[Viti panting, coughing]

13:57.545 --> 14:00.006
I can't guarantee you'll get
one of these, uh,

14:00.674 --> 14:02.967
gold nameplates,
but I'm sure we can find you

14:03.093 --> 14:05.303
a very nice unmarked hole
somewhere.

14:07.847 --> 14:09.891
She-She was gonna leave him,
you know...

14:11.518 --> 14:12.894
The night Isabella died.

14:14.020 --> 14:15.522
She was gonna leave Carmine.

14:16.439 --> 14:18.024
Don't talk about my mother.

14:18.149 --> 14:19.567
[Viti] You remember, don't you?

14:19.567 --> 14:21.111
You were all packed
and ready to go.

14:21.111 --> 14:23.988
She was gonna take you
and your brother on a trip.

14:25.281 --> 14:26.408
That's what she told you.

14:28.159 --> 14:29.786
She was my cousin.

14:29.786 --> 14:30.829
I loved her.

14:30.954 --> 14:32.372
She asked for my help.

14:33.039 --> 14:36.334
I had a fucking car waiting
a few blocks down the road

14:36.459 --> 14:37.877
and she never fuckin' showed.

14:38.378 --> 14:39.421
[Viti choking]

14:39.421 --> 14:43.216
You are a desperate
fucking liar.

14:43.341 --> 14:44.342
I swear.

14:45.719 --> 14:47.387
I got no reason to lie anymore!

14:48.179 --> 14:50.348
[Viti coughs]

14:53.309 --> 14:55.061
I ain't tryin' to push
on a bruise, Sofia.

14:57.480 --> 14:59.357
She was with Carmine
'cause of me.

15:00.358 --> 15:01.609
You knew that, right?

15:02.360 --> 15:03.445
I introduced them.

15:05.363 --> 15:06.698
And your father.

15:06.823 --> 15:08.867
He was smitten
right outta the gate.

15:09.868 --> 15:12.037
God, she was beautiful,
your mom.

15:12.162 --> 15:14.414
[emotional, uneasy music
playing]

15:14.539 --> 15:16.249
She was so beautiful.

15:18.209 --> 15:20.045
She had that laugh.
When you got her going,

15:20.170 --> 15:21.379
it'd knock you out.

15:22.839 --> 15:24.049
[laughs softly]

15:25.759 --> 15:28.261
She couldn't take it anymore
being his wife.

15:29.721 --> 15:31.431
She just fucking
couldn't take it.

15:33.183 --> 15:37.228
She tried to leave once before,
but she came right back.

15:38.730 --> 15:41.649
She came right back
'cause of you fucking kids.

15:42.734 --> 15:44.194
Would've been so much
easier for her

15:44.194 --> 15:45.904
if it weren't
for the two of you.

15:46.780 --> 15:48.823
[music darkens]

15:51.034 --> 15:52.911
[barrel scraping]

15:53.036 --> 15:54.871
[Viti shivering]

15:55.580 --> 15:58.583
[Viti] I wi...
Sometimes, I wish...

16:00.919 --> 16:01.920
It's done.

16:03.421 --> 16:05.215
What's done is... [shivers]

16:05.215 --> 16:07.300
What's done is done.
What he did is done.

16:08.051 --> 16:10.345
[sighs, shivers]

16:10.345 --> 16:12.430
But you kept on working for him.

16:13.598 --> 16:17.102
You loved her so much, you were
his underboss for years.

16:18.978 --> 16:20.146
Yeah.

16:21.064 --> 16:23.483
- [Viti sighs, shivers]
- Yeah.

16:25.944 --> 16:27.696
But you need me now, Sofia.

16:28.238 --> 16:29.489
You need me.

16:29.948 --> 16:32.701
You wanna be boss?
You wanna win this war?

16:32.701 --> 16:35.370
Then money's not enough.
You need respect.

16:35.370 --> 16:37.872
You need soldiers
who want to fight for you.

16:37.872 --> 16:40.333
You go it alone out there,
you're not gonna last a day.

16:40.917 --> 16:42.627
I can get you that respect.

16:43.461 --> 16:45.005
I couldn't help your mother.

16:46.965 --> 16:47.966
Let me help you.

16:49.175 --> 16:51.219
[Viti gasping]

16:52.512 --> 16:53.471
Come on.

16:54.764 --> 16:56.307
[lock clicking]

16:56.433 --> 16:58.309
[TV playing indistinctly]

16:59.602 --> 17:00.770
Mrs. Cobb?

17:00.770 --> 17:02.230
[woman on TV]
What are you gonna do?

17:02.230 --> 17:04.024
Shoot a six-year-old kid...

17:04.024 --> 17:05.608
- [door closes, lock clicks]
- It's...

17:05.608 --> 17:08.069
- [engine revs on TV]
- [man exclaims on TV]

17:08.069 --> 17:09.487
[tires screeching on TV]

17:09.612 --> 17:11.990
- Mrs. Cobb, it's... it's Victor.
- [gunfire on TV]

17:14.993 --> 17:16.995
- [TV audio mutes]
- Francis?

17:17.954 --> 17:19.497
[uneasy music playing]

17:28.465 --> 17:30.175
[faint hissing]

17:31.551 --> 17:33.386
[whispers] Oh my God...

17:34.304 --> 17:36.181
- [pots clanging]
- [Victor reacts in pain]

17:38.516 --> 17:39.684
[hissing stops]

17:48.860 --> 17:50.737
[uneasy music continues]

17:55.033 --> 17:56.993
- Mrs. Cobb?
- [music fades]

17:56.993 --> 17:58.203
Hey.

17:58.745 --> 18:01.039
- [Victor] Hi.
- Hey. There you are.

18:01.831 --> 18:04.584
[laughs] Why are you
way over there?

18:04.709 --> 18:06.378
Come here, sweetheart.

18:07.671 --> 18:09.798
Come here. [laughs]

18:10.507 --> 18:11.883
Look what I found.

18:12.592 --> 18:14.052
You remember this?

18:14.177 --> 18:16.179
Um... no.

18:16.179 --> 18:17.430
No, ma'am.

18:17.430 --> 18:19.891
It's your glove
from Little League.

18:20.016 --> 18:22.602
- Look how small--
- I'm sorry. I'm...

18:22.727 --> 18:24.437
I'm V... [stammers]

18:25.397 --> 18:27.482
I'm V-Victor.

18:27.482 --> 18:28.650
I'm Victor.

18:29.693 --> 18:31.861
[stutters] I-I work with Oz.

18:31.861 --> 18:34.280
Oswald... Right? Your son?

18:34.280 --> 18:37.659
He-He s-sent me here
to ch-check up on you.

18:37.659 --> 18:39.285
I know who you are.

18:40.787 --> 18:43.415
I tell my son to visit more,
so he sends strangers.

18:45.625 --> 18:46.584
I get it.

18:49.587 --> 18:51.923
Well, help me up
for Christ's sake.

18:56.803 --> 18:59.472
Uh, okay, here we go.

18:59.597 --> 19:00.432
Whoa, whoa.

19:01.599 --> 19:02.684
What is this?

19:02.684 --> 19:04.269
What? I don't know.

19:04.769 --> 19:06.521
Oh, shit. Well...

19:06.521 --> 19:07.605
I fell.

19:09.232 --> 19:11.776
Maybe I was pushed. [laughs]

19:15.613 --> 19:16.781
So...

19:18.783 --> 19:20.285
- Nurse boy.
- [Victor groans]

19:20.410 --> 19:22.954
What's Oswald doin' that's more
important than me? Huh?

19:23.079 --> 19:24.789
He's making a move, um...

19:26.082 --> 19:27.917
against the Maronis.

19:27.917 --> 19:30.128
- Maronis?
- [food thuds in garbage can]

19:30.253 --> 19:32.172
No, baby, you got it backwards.

19:32.297 --> 19:34.341
He's workin' them to get
at the Falcones.

19:34.341 --> 19:36.217
- [plate clatters]
- They're the bigger fish.

19:38.428 --> 19:39.637
They're all dead.

19:42.474 --> 19:44.642
Was it him? Did Oswald kill 'em?

19:48.355 --> 19:49.481
Yeah.

19:50.482 --> 19:51.691
Don't lie to me.

19:52.525 --> 19:53.693
You're bad at it.

19:54.819 --> 19:55.904
It's the truth.

19:58.948 --> 19:59.866
Oz...

20:01.284 --> 20:02.994
Oz pulled this off.

20:03.119 --> 20:05.413
That's why I'm here right now,
to... to...

20:05.413 --> 20:08.792
m-make sure that you're safe

20:08.792 --> 20:10.335
while this is all going down.

20:11.169 --> 20:12.545
[Francis] Finally.

20:13.213 --> 20:14.506
Okay, then. [sniffles]

20:14.631 --> 20:15.590
So...

20:16.508 --> 20:18.885
he's gonna need
my help then, right?

20:20.345 --> 20:22.722
Okay, let's go! Let's do this!

20:22.847 --> 20:24.349
Let's... [cackles]

20:24.474 --> 20:26.643
[dramatic music playing]

20:26.643 --> 20:28.937
[prisoners clamoring]

20:38.697 --> 20:40.532
[prisoner yelling indistinctly]

20:41.324 --> 20:42.951
[tap running]

20:42.951 --> 20:44.577
[cell door sliding]

20:45.370 --> 20:46.830
- [tap stops]
- [approaching footsteps]

20:46.830 --> 20:48.623
[Mikey] This is from Oz, motherfucker.

20:48.623 --> 20:50.250
- [grunting]
- [suspenseful music plays]

20:51.167 --> 20:53.294
[Salvatore groaning]

21:11.688 --> 21:13.231
[music fades]

21:17.777 --> 21:19.237
[engine stops]

21:20.030 --> 21:21.489
Nadia, Nadia, Nadia.

21:22.240 --> 21:23.408
Always a pleasure.

21:24.701 --> 21:26.411
My son. Now.

21:27.203 --> 21:29.873
Straight to business, huh?
You know, I respect that.

21:31.875 --> 21:33.626
- Bruno.
- [van door opens]

21:34.753 --> 21:36.254
[thudding in van]

21:36.796 --> 21:37.839
[Oz] C'mere.

21:37.839 --> 21:39.424
[muffled grunting]

21:39.549 --> 21:41.801
[Oz] Jesus.
Stop fuckin' shakin'.

21:45.764 --> 21:47.390
[van door creaks shut]

21:47.390 --> 21:49.059
What have you done to him?

21:49.059 --> 21:52.020
He's fine. Picture of health.

21:52.020 --> 21:54.439
Remove the tape.
I want to hear it from him.

21:55.065 --> 21:57.067
I'm doing you a solid.
Your son's a talker.

21:57.067 --> 21:58.568
We all want this over quick.

21:58.568 --> 22:02.030
Just lemme see the shrooms,
and we'll be on our way.

22:02.030 --> 22:04.282
- [Taj grunting]
- [liquid dripping]

22:04.908 --> 22:06.659
Bruno. Check the product.

22:06.785 --> 22:09.037
[tense music playing]

22:17.754 --> 22:19.798
- [muffled whimpers]
- Calm down.

22:19.923 --> 22:23.009
- Relax. Jesus Christ.
- [liquid dripping]

22:23.134 --> 22:24.386
We're good.

22:24.386 --> 22:26.179
Alright, Nadia.

22:26.304 --> 22:28.014
My friend Bruno,
he's gonna get in that truck--

22:28.139 --> 22:29.808
That truck stays put...

22:31.434 --> 22:32.644
until my son is released.

22:32.769 --> 22:34.270
Relax, Nadia.

22:34.270 --> 22:35.480
I know.

22:38.441 --> 22:39.526
Go to Mama.

22:40.985 --> 22:43.029
[muffled grunting]

22:45.156 --> 22:47.033
[breathing heavily]

22:47.158 --> 22:49.077
[muffled grunting]

22:51.871 --> 22:53.123
So sorry...

22:53.123 --> 22:54.541
- [gate closing]
- [alarm blaring]

22:54.541 --> 22:56.793
- [Oz] Fuck!
- [suspenseful music plays]

22:56.793 --> 22:59.337
[gunfire]

22:59.462 --> 23:00.880
[grunting]

23:00.880 --> 23:02.173
[Taj grunting]

23:05.010 --> 23:07.095
- [gunfire continues]
- [man grunts]

23:08.179 --> 23:09.514
[grunting]

23:10.807 --> 23:11.683
[lighter clicks]

23:15.395 --> 23:16.521
- [Nadia] Baby...
- [Taj] Mom.

23:18.064 --> 23:18.940
Oh, no.

23:18.940 --> 23:20.650
Oh, shit!

23:20.650 --> 23:23.111
[Taj screaming]

23:23.111 --> 23:25.572
[Taj continues screaming]

23:25.697 --> 23:27.824
[tense, dramatic music playing]

23:27.824 --> 23:29.951
[both screaming]

23:34.706 --> 23:39.044
[screaming continues]

23:42.213 --> 23:44.549
[fire suppressors hissing]

23:44.674 --> 23:46.509
[alarm ringing]

23:46.509 --> 23:48.553
[hissing]

23:48.678 --> 23:50.096
[Oz] Fuck! The shrooms!

23:50.096 --> 23:51.765
Get in the truck!

23:54.517 --> 23:56.353
- Go, go, go!
- [tires screeching]

23:56.353 --> 23:59.439
["De Do Do Do, De Da Da Da"
by The Police playing]

24:01.441 --> 24:05.445
♪ ...Their logic ties you up
and rapes you ♪

24:07.697 --> 24:10.742
♪ De do do do, de da da da ♪

24:10.867 --> 24:13.578
♪ Is all I want to say to you ♪

24:14.162 --> 24:17.332
♪ De do do do, de da da da ♪

24:17.332 --> 24:20.251
♪ Their innocence
will pull me through ♪

24:20.835 --> 24:23.505
♪ De do do do, de da da da ♪

24:23.505 --> 24:25.256
- [music stops]
- [Nick] Shit, what happened?

24:25.382 --> 24:27.384
- You alright?
- [Bruno] It was fucked up, man.

24:27.384 --> 24:29.928
They tried to screw us.
Oz lit 'em up...

24:30.053 --> 24:32.806
[conversation continues
indistinctly]

24:33.598 --> 24:35.433
No, no, no.

24:35.558 --> 24:36.434
No!

24:37.602 --> 24:38.853
No, no, no...

24:40.438 --> 24:41.272
No.

24:42.440 --> 24:43.942
No!

24:45.610 --> 24:46.945
Fuckin' dead.

24:47.070 --> 24:47.904
Fuck.

24:48.405 --> 24:49.864
They're all fuckin' dead!

24:52.992 --> 24:53.868
That's it?!

24:53.868 --> 24:55.578
Oz? What-What's the matter?

24:55.578 --> 24:58.289
They're ruined.
We got two buckets.

24:58.790 --> 24:59.624
That's fuckin' it!

24:59.749 --> 25:01.418
The rest are fucked!

25:01.418 --> 25:04.379
You don't build a goddamn empire
with two fuckin' buckets!

25:04.379 --> 25:06.339
- We can't get more?
- More?

25:06.339 --> 25:08.216
- Yeah.
- From where, Nick? Huh?

25:08.967 --> 25:10.635
Sofia's been working this shit
for months.

25:11.594 --> 25:13.847
Take these to the truck.
Get this shit.

25:14.514 --> 25:16.391
Crank up the heat.
Keep 'em warm.

25:16.391 --> 25:19.310
[phone buzzing]

25:20.520 --> 25:21.980
[Nick] Put them in the back
of the van.

25:22.105 --> 25:24.190
I'll start the engine
and turn on the heat.

25:24.983 --> 25:26.943
Mikey, tell me somethin' good.

25:26.943 --> 25:28.820
[Salvatore] Mikey's dead,
you little bitch.

25:28.945 --> 25:30.321
[ominous music playing]

25:30.447 --> 25:31.990
Thanks for the keys, Oz.

25:32.115 --> 25:34.659
I never coulda busted out
without 'em.

25:35.452 --> 25:37.871
[scoffs] You amateur
piece of shit.

25:39.289 --> 25:41.708
There's no place
I can't find you now.

25:42.500 --> 25:43.835
No place, Oz!

25:45.670 --> 25:46.838
You are cooked.

25:46.963 --> 25:48.256
Cooked, huh?

25:50.008 --> 25:51.009
That's funny.

25:51.718 --> 25:52.886
Do me a favor, Sal.

25:53.553 --> 25:54.554
Call your wife.

25:55.138 --> 25:56.348
See if she answers.

26:00.018 --> 26:02.103
You stole
from the wrong fucking guy.

26:03.730 --> 26:05.774
- [music fades]
- [panting]

26:06.900 --> 26:08.068
Fuck.

26:12.697 --> 26:15.200
[line ringing]

26:18.328 --> 26:20.121
- [Victor] Oz.
- How is she?

26:20.705 --> 26:22.957
Yeah, uh, no,
she's-she's... she's...

26:23.750 --> 26:24.668
She's f--

26:24.668 --> 26:26.086
Vic, how is she?!

26:26.086 --> 26:28.046
She's fine.
She's just-- She's sleeping.

26:29.923 --> 26:31.216
When you gonna be here?

26:33.718 --> 26:35.428
Look, I got a lotta heat on me.

26:35.553 --> 26:36.805
So, uh...

26:39.057 --> 26:41.685
I need you to get my ma
outta there, alright?

26:41.685 --> 26:42.977
There's a go bag in the kitchen,

26:42.977 --> 26:45.021
it's behind the vent,
in the pantry.

26:45.021 --> 26:47.023
Take it and whatever else
you can get. Her meds.

26:47.023 --> 26:49.567
Don't forget her fucking meds!
She ain't gonna like it much.

26:49.693 --> 26:51.486
- You seen how she can get.
- Wh...

26:52.862 --> 26:54.572
- What happened?
- Goddammit, Vic!

26:54.698 --> 26:55.990
Just do it, alright?

26:56.741 --> 26:59.119
W-Well, where do we go?

27:00.120 --> 27:01.830
[uneasy music playing]

27:03.456 --> 27:04.499
I don't know.

27:06.292 --> 27:09.838
It's gotta be somewhere
where nobody'd think to look.

27:09.838 --> 27:11.256
You know?

27:11.381 --> 27:13.842
Just, uh... Just get in the car.

27:14.384 --> 27:15.343
Right? And just drive.

27:15.343 --> 27:17.595
Okay, yeah.
I'll-I'll-I'll-I'll...

27:17.721 --> 27:19.931
[breathes rapidly]
I'll find a place that's safe.

27:20.056 --> 27:22.684
And, uh, I'll call you
when I get there, alright?

27:23.226 --> 27:24.978
- Yeah, good, good.
- Okay. Hey, Oz.

27:26.229 --> 27:28.189
I got this, okay?

27:30.442 --> 27:31.943
I'm gonna take care of her.

27:32.444 --> 27:33.611
Yeah, you do that.

27:38.074 --> 27:39.409
[music fades]

27:39.409 --> 27:41.036
[birds singing]

27:50.128 --> 27:52.005
[sniffing softly]

27:52.589 --> 27:54.341
["Reckless" by St. Vincent
playing]

27:54.466 --> 27:55.633
[knocking]

27:57.260 --> 27:58.303
Yes?

28:02.682 --> 28:03.683
[Julian] Sofia...

28:13.610 --> 28:14.986
[door closes]

28:15.528 --> 28:16.905
What are you doing here?

28:19.866 --> 28:21.159
[Julian] The police came to me,

28:21.868 --> 28:23.203
asking about you.

28:24.162 --> 28:25.038
[Sofia] Hmm.

28:25.997 --> 28:27.248
I didn't say anything.

28:28.541 --> 28:29.876
What do you want, Julian?

28:30.543 --> 28:32.295
Because I'm in the middle
of something,

28:32.295 --> 28:34.839
and I think we're past the point
of analysis, don't you?

28:36.508 --> 28:37.676
Yes.

28:39.386 --> 28:40.512
You're right.

28:43.223 --> 28:44.766
And you were right about me.

28:48.186 --> 28:49.688
But it's not the control I miss.

28:52.315 --> 28:53.692
When I saw what happened
on the news,

28:53.817 --> 28:54.818
I knew it was you.

28:56.903 --> 28:58.738
That you did what you had to do.

29:00.532 --> 29:01.908
I can already see it,

29:02.701 --> 29:03.868
what it's given you.

29:05.662 --> 29:06.788
The release.

29:09.833 --> 29:11.543
And I'd like to feel that, too.

29:12.836 --> 29:13.920
With you.

29:16.548 --> 29:18.550
I'd like to be a part
of whatever's next...

29:19.426 --> 29:21.094
[music builds]

29:22.095 --> 29:23.638
...if you'll have me.

29:30.395 --> 29:32.230
[music intensifies]

29:32.355 --> 29:34.149
[men chattering]

29:36.484 --> 29:38.653
♪ Calling for me ♪

29:38.653 --> 29:39.821
[Viti] Hey!

29:40.905 --> 29:42.282
Quiet the fuck down.

29:44.743 --> 29:46.411
The lady's got something to say.

29:46.911 --> 29:48.955
["Reckless" continues playing]

29:54.419 --> 29:56.171
♪ Calling for me ♪

29:57.255 --> 29:58.965
♪ Calling for me ♪

30:02.427 --> 30:04.262
[Sofia] Thank you, Johnny.

30:06.931 --> 30:07.891
[Viti] Sit down.

30:07.891 --> 30:09.309
[music fades]

30:12.729 --> 30:13.938
[Viti clears throat]

30:14.647 --> 30:16.149
[Sofia] First,
I'd like to address

30:16.149 --> 30:17.692
the elephant in the room.

30:19.319 --> 30:20.862
I gassed the Family.

30:20.862 --> 30:23.031
[man whispers] Oh, Jesus Christ.

30:26.826 --> 30:28.370
I killed them all.

30:30.455 --> 30:31.498
And I am

30:32.332 --> 30:34.000
so glad

30:34.668 --> 30:35.627
that they're dead.

30:36.961 --> 30:41.007
My family disposed of my mother
like she was nothing.

30:41.132 --> 30:43.134
Then they did the same to me.

30:44.177 --> 30:45.178
And honestly,

30:46.971 --> 30:48.056
none of you

30:48.807 --> 30:50.141
are any different.

30:52.310 --> 30:54.896
None of you are made men.

30:56.272 --> 30:57.732
Except for Johnny here.

30:58.817 --> 30:59.651
[kisses]

31:01.027 --> 31:02.153
The rest of you...

31:04.280 --> 31:05.407
[inhales sharply]

31:05.407 --> 31:06.825
You're pawns.

31:08.702 --> 31:09.994
You're overlooked.

31:11.162 --> 31:12.372
Expendable.

31:12.872 --> 31:14.499
[uneasy music playing]

31:15.709 --> 31:19.170
My mother was Isabella Gigante.

31:19.295 --> 31:20.630
[inhales shakily]

31:20.630 --> 31:23.008
Few spoke of her after she died,

31:23.675 --> 31:26.094
because she was a force

31:26.886 --> 31:30.515
greater than the Falcones
could handle.

31:33.059 --> 31:34.227
As of today,

31:35.020 --> 31:37.397
my father's legacy is dead

31:37.522 --> 31:41.609
and we will never speak
his name again.

31:42.193 --> 31:44.029
From this point on,

31:45.238 --> 31:46.906
I am a Gigante,

31:47.866 --> 31:50.452
and this is a new Family now.

31:50.452 --> 31:51.953
[hushed] What are you doing?

31:51.953 --> 31:56.499
A family that will not treat you
like cannon fodder

31:56.499 --> 31:59.502
in a fruitless war
against the Maronis.

31:59.502 --> 32:01.379
A war which I intend to end.

32:01.504 --> 32:03.048
Alright, okay, Sofia.

32:04.174 --> 32:06.676
Let's not be rash here.
These gentlemen know

32:06.676 --> 32:08.219
we got a score
we need to settle--

32:09.220 --> 32:11.056
[men gasping]

32:12.098 --> 32:15.060
[whispering indistinctly]

32:15.185 --> 32:16.227
[Sofia] Hmm.

32:16.353 --> 32:17.645
[Sofia huffs]

32:27.280 --> 32:28.239
This.

32:29.199 --> 32:30.492
This was my father's.

32:31.534 --> 32:33.620
But he made it off
of your labor.

32:34.788 --> 32:37.415
You did the dirty work

32:38.208 --> 32:40.585
and they kept it all
for themselves.

32:43.380 --> 32:44.839
If you join me,

32:46.591 --> 32:48.635
you will have a new Family.

32:50.428 --> 32:53.348
And I'll pay you
what you're worth.

32:53.932 --> 32:56.518
More money than
you've ever seen before.

32:56.518 --> 32:58.603
[tense music playing]

33:05.735 --> 33:07.195
[inhales deeply]

33:07.195 --> 33:08.488
[sighs]

33:13.451 --> 33:14.452
Ms. Gigante?

33:22.085 --> 33:23.044
Go ahead.

33:24.295 --> 33:27.716
[dramatic music playing]

33:34.347 --> 33:36.850
[dramatic music swells,
fades out]

33:36.850 --> 33:39.686
- [siren wailing]
- [car horn honking]

33:42.772 --> 33:45.525
- [siren continues]
- [car horns honking]

33:49.279 --> 33:51.990
[siren chirping]

33:52.490 --> 33:54.492
[kids chattering]

33:55.618 --> 33:56.911
[Francis] Why are we here?

33:57.537 --> 33:59.664
You said Oswald was takin' over.

34:00.290 --> 34:02.208
Yeah, he is, but, uh...

34:02.208 --> 34:04.461
He said things
with the Maronis got messy

34:04.461 --> 34:08.173
and that we should go somewhere
no one would think to look.

34:08.798 --> 34:09.924
[man] All right, let's go.

34:10.842 --> 34:12.427
Clean 'em out. Take everything.

34:12.427 --> 34:14.929
Whatever's left of this
fucking shithole.

34:14.929 --> 34:16.556
[indistinct chatter]

34:19.642 --> 34:21.770
No one really cares about
Crown Point, so...

34:21.770 --> 34:22.937
[engine stops]

34:24.898 --> 34:27.650
[hip-hop music playing
in background]

34:27.650 --> 34:30.028
[distant siren wailing]

34:33.490 --> 34:34.366
[car door opens]

34:38.328 --> 34:39.537
Ain't this nice.

34:40.538 --> 34:42.082
VIP parkin'.

34:42.082 --> 34:44.292
[man] We're gonna smash
this shit right here.

34:46.211 --> 34:48.004
- Grab everything that's left.
- [glass smashing]

34:48.004 --> 34:49.297
Don't leave nothin' in there.

34:49.297 --> 34:51.299
Clean the whole
fuckin' place out.

34:52.384 --> 34:55.095
[glass clinking]

34:55.220 --> 34:56.388
Shit.

34:58.431 --> 35:00.934
[bottles clinking]

35:01.726 --> 35:03.061
[whispers] Hey. Whoa.

35:03.895 --> 35:05.730
Don't let 'em see you, okay?
Come on.

35:08.942 --> 35:10.318
Come on. Come on.

35:11.361 --> 35:13.571
- Come on.
- What did he do to you?

35:14.531 --> 35:16.157
You're practically
pissin' yourself.

35:16.157 --> 35:17.659
Please. Shut up. Shut up.
Shut up.

35:17.659 --> 35:19.285
Come here, come on.

35:19.285 --> 35:20.578
Come on, come on, come on.

35:24.457 --> 35:25.458
Please.

35:26.418 --> 35:27.585
His name...

35:28.211 --> 35:29.462
His name is S-Squid.

35:29.462 --> 35:31.006
He's a bad guy.

35:31.006 --> 35:34.009
He runs, uh, Drops and all
the other stuff in this area.

35:35.135 --> 35:36.553
Listen, Francis.

35:36.553 --> 35:38.596
We gotta get off of the street
right now, okay?

35:39.389 --> 35:41.099
That's where we're headed.
You ready?

35:43.560 --> 35:45.437
[glass clinking]

35:46.146 --> 35:48.023
[Francis] Where are you
takin' me?

35:48.023 --> 35:49.941
[Victor] My friend Calvin's
apartment.

35:51.234 --> 35:52.485
He used to live here.

35:52.485 --> 35:53.820
Watch your step.

35:53.945 --> 35:55.613
It's been condemned.

35:56.948 --> 35:57.949
Come on.

35:58.074 --> 36:00.160
[hip-hop music
continues faintly]

36:04.122 --> 36:05.790
[ominous music playing]

36:15.467 --> 36:16.634
[music fades]

36:18.011 --> 36:20.013
[door hinge creaking]

36:27.812 --> 36:29.230
No lights, huh?

36:31.691 --> 36:32.650
Yeah.

36:42.994 --> 36:44.579
[Francis sighs]

36:46.331 --> 36:47.415
[Francis] Wow.

36:50.335 --> 36:51.836
[Victor] What is it?
What's wrong?

36:54.506 --> 36:57.175
This looks like the apartment
I had with my boys.

37:00.679 --> 37:01.930
I hate it here.

37:03.306 --> 37:05.350
[soft, melancholy music playing]

37:15.485 --> 37:16.945
I used to live over there.

37:18.863 --> 37:20.407
[sighs]

37:20.532 --> 37:22.701
The Eastside is cursed.

37:27.914 --> 37:29.833
It takes everything from you.

37:34.212 --> 37:36.756
[subway clattering]

37:36.756 --> 37:38.591
[indistinct yelling]

37:39.592 --> 37:40.719
[whistling]

37:41.553 --> 37:43.471
[pounding on door]

37:44.222 --> 37:46.558
[soft pop music playing
on stereo]

37:48.935 --> 37:50.061
You alone?

37:50.186 --> 37:51.980
- What's wrong?
- [lock clicks]

37:51.980 --> 37:53.732
[breathing rapidly]

37:56.526 --> 37:58.987
Oz, baby.
What have they done to you?

38:00.572 --> 38:02.741
- Hey. Hey. Okay.
- Come here.

38:02.866 --> 38:04.701
[Eve] It's okay. It's okay.

38:04.701 --> 38:06.369
[Oz] Alright, get your things.

38:06.369 --> 38:07.620
Come on.

38:08.621 --> 38:10.582
We gotta lay low.
Vic's already in Crown Point.

38:10.707 --> 38:12.000
He's got us a nice spot
by the Zoo.

38:12.000 --> 38:13.501
Crown Point?
What are you talking about?

38:13.501 --> 38:15.045
I know it ain't perfect.

38:15.045 --> 38:16.921
It's the only place
Sal and Sofia got no pull.

38:17.047 --> 38:18.465
Sal? Oh my God, Oz.

38:18.465 --> 38:20.759
There's something else.
Before we go, I gotta tell ya.

38:20.884 --> 38:22.469
It ain't just me and Vic, alright?

38:22.594 --> 38:23.636
Yeah, but, Oz.

38:23.762 --> 38:25.930
I'm not-- I'm not going
with you.

38:27.766 --> 38:28.850
I can't.

38:29.559 --> 38:31.436
I thought we was
in this together.

38:32.937 --> 38:35.190
Un-fuckin'-believable,
you're doing this right now.

38:36.399 --> 38:38.151
Where you gonna go, huh?

38:38.151 --> 38:40.779
You got some high roller
you'd rather shack up with, huh?

38:40.904 --> 38:42.364
- For the money?
- Oz. Baby.

38:42.364 --> 38:43.615
We had a deal.

38:44.324 --> 38:46.951
We look out for each other.
We don't fuck each other over.

38:47.660 --> 38:49.204
That's why this worked.

38:49.788 --> 38:50.705
It ain't--

38:52.290 --> 38:54.084
After everything I done for you?

38:54.084 --> 38:56.044
It ain't fucking workin'
no more?

38:56.044 --> 38:59.339
Huh? After everything
I fucking done for you?

38:59.464 --> 39:01.299
Jesus fucking Christ!

39:02.425 --> 39:03.677
Fuck.

39:03.677 --> 39:05.387
I'm a fuckin' idiot!

39:06.471 --> 39:08.390
- Fuckin' dumb.
- Okay, okay. Shh.

39:08.390 --> 39:11.142
- Stupid. Stupid.
- No, no, no, no, no, no.

39:11.267 --> 39:12.644
[ominous music playing]

39:12.769 --> 39:14.187
You're onto something, baby.

39:18.525 --> 39:21.236
I know you gonna be
on top again soon.

39:29.494 --> 39:30.995
You know I'm yours.

39:33.957 --> 39:35.375
But right now, I'm just...

39:35.375 --> 39:37.168
I'm just gonna hold you back.

39:42.173 --> 39:44.342
[exhales, sighs]

39:46.177 --> 39:48.680
- [insects chirring]
- [music fades]

39:49.848 --> 39:51.850
[vehicle approaching]

39:52.517 --> 39:54.019
[crying softly]

39:56.813 --> 39:58.189
[sniffles]

39:58.982 --> 40:00.358
[vehicle doors open]

40:00.483 --> 40:02.110
[man] Shit! Around the back!

40:02.110 --> 40:04.320
- [gunfire outside]
- [man yells in pain]

40:04.320 --> 40:06.031
- [gunshot]
- [body thuds]

40:14.914 --> 40:15.957
[door closes]

40:18.209 --> 40:20.795
Freedom always comes at a cost,
doesn't it?

40:21.588 --> 40:23.715
[grunting in pain]

40:24.674 --> 40:25.884
Sit down, Salvatore.

40:33.683 --> 40:35.226
What a funky hideout.

40:40.523 --> 40:42.108
Big fan of wood, I see.

40:44.736 --> 40:45.987
Ooh!

40:45.987 --> 40:47.739
Oh, Antonucci's.

40:48.406 --> 40:50.492
Oh, that doesn't look like
it traveled well.

40:56.373 --> 40:58.792
My father always said you were
too sentimental.

40:59.626 --> 41:00.835
That it made you weak.

41:02.754 --> 41:04.297
I don't think he understood

41:05.048 --> 41:07.759
why you cared so much
about your family.

41:08.426 --> 41:11.304
That's because you Falcones
eat your own.

41:12.764 --> 41:15.141
Your family had it right,
I think.

41:17.435 --> 41:18.478
Ten years ago,

41:18.603 --> 41:19.813
some measly driver

41:20.397 --> 41:22.273
spun a bullshit story about me.

41:23.108 --> 41:24.609
He betrayed me,

41:24.734 --> 41:26.403
the daughter of the Falcone Don,

41:26.403 --> 41:28.363
and he got rewarded for it.

41:29.239 --> 41:30.782
And now here we are.

41:32.283 --> 41:35.453
Both of us suffering
at the hands of that same man.

41:36.663 --> 41:38.206
[breathes shakily]

41:38.206 --> 41:39.374
But you...

41:41.960 --> 41:43.670
Would you have let that stand?

41:44.337 --> 41:45.255
[scoffs]

41:46.131 --> 41:49.426
I woulda ripped out his tongue
and left him for the vultures.

41:49.426 --> 41:50.969
That's what I thought.

41:55.682 --> 41:57.976
I'm very sorry about your wife
and son, Salvatore.

41:58.101 --> 42:00.186
Why are you here?
What do you want?

42:00.812 --> 42:03.565
I've come here to end the war
between our Families.

42:03.565 --> 42:04.858
[exhales]

42:11.823 --> 42:13.533
[tense music playing]

42:14.826 --> 42:16.369
I'm not gonna kill you.

42:17.328 --> 42:18.246
Why?

42:19.998 --> 42:22.167
Because it's what Oz wants.

42:23.126 --> 42:24.836
Ah, Falcones and Maronis
have been--

42:24.961 --> 42:27.589
The Falcones
don't exist anymore.

42:28.506 --> 42:30.342
I am offering you an alliance.

42:31.384 --> 42:32.719
We join our families,

42:32.844 --> 42:35.180
the Maronis and Gigantes,

42:35.847 --> 42:37.515
as a show of strength.

42:39.017 --> 42:40.018
We kill Oz.

42:41.019 --> 42:42.604
And then we take over the city.

42:42.604 --> 42:43.855
[dramatic music builds]

42:45.398 --> 42:46.274
Together.

42:47.734 --> 42:48.777
[music fades]

42:50.236 --> 42:51.363
[door opens]

42:54.407 --> 42:55.575
[door closes]

43:24.229 --> 43:26.648
[distant siren wailing]

43:47.585 --> 43:48.920
[bed frame squeaks]

43:56.761 --> 43:58.513
[Oz whispers softly]

44:00.140 --> 44:01.933
Oswald...

44:07.731 --> 44:08.940
[softly] I'm sorry, Ma.

44:09.899 --> 44:11.484
I feel like I let you down.

44:12.777 --> 44:13.778
You did.

44:18.241 --> 44:19.617
This place is temporary.

44:19.743 --> 44:21.578
- I got...
- [chuckles]

44:21.578 --> 44:23.705
I just gotta figure out
my next move.

44:24.789 --> 44:25.707
Yep.

44:26.833 --> 44:28.835
My boy... [sniffles]

44:28.960 --> 44:30.545
With such big dreams.

44:30.545 --> 44:31.880
[Oz chuckles]

44:32.339 --> 44:33.548
Like your father.

44:35.467 --> 44:36.718
No, Ma.

44:38.428 --> 44:39.804
I ain't like him.

44:40.680 --> 44:42.640
- I can fix this.
- [Francis murmurs]

44:44.267 --> 44:46.478
It's you and me
under one roof now.

44:47.103 --> 44:48.480
Like it used to be.

44:52.942 --> 44:54.361
Are you're tryin' to kill me?

44:55.278 --> 44:57.072
No, Ma,
I'm tryin' to protect you.

45:00.492 --> 45:01.743
It's better this way,

45:02.535 --> 45:03.828
when we're together.

45:04.496 --> 45:05.747
Takin' me back here,

45:07.165 --> 45:08.833
you're throwin' it in my face...

45:09.876 --> 45:11.252
what I lost.

45:16.216 --> 45:17.509
I lost 'em too.

45:24.182 --> 45:25.225
[Francis sniffles]

45:27.519 --> 45:30.355
What kind of man can't take care
of his own mother?

45:32.023 --> 45:33.191
Get off.

45:38.488 --> 45:39.614
Get off!

45:43.326 --> 45:44.744
[sniffling]

45:46.162 --> 45:48.039
[sighs]

45:55.672 --> 45:56.715
[door closes]

46:03.179 --> 46:04.556
[glass clinking]

46:10.395 --> 46:11.771
[objects clattering]

46:11.771 --> 46:13.023
[Victor] I'm awake.

46:13.023 --> 46:14.107
[Oz] Hey.

46:14.232 --> 46:15.900
[exhales] Fuck. Oz...

46:16.735 --> 46:19.571
Shit. I fell asleep.
Alright, I'm--

46:19.696 --> 46:20.739
[Oz] Stop.

46:25.577 --> 46:26.661
You did good, kid.

46:29.205 --> 46:31.166
I know you don't wanna be
here neither.

46:31.166 --> 46:32.417
It was a smart move.

46:33.251 --> 46:34.669
Crown Point.

46:38.089 --> 46:40.008
[traffic hums outside]

46:40.008 --> 46:42.177
[distant siren wailing]

46:44.095 --> 46:46.598
[people chattering outside]

46:48.099 --> 46:49.976
Told her I'd get her
a penthouse.

46:51.811 --> 46:53.104
The best view in the city.

46:53.730 --> 46:56.232
[Victor] She s-said that
you guys

46:56.232 --> 46:59.110
kinda lived near here?

47:00.111 --> 47:01.780
[Oz] Two-bedroom walk-up.

47:03.782 --> 47:05.950
Looked a helluva lot
like this fuckin' dump.

47:12.290 --> 47:13.333
[chuckles]

47:14.751 --> 47:16.127
This was Jack's.

47:17.629 --> 47:18.838
Benny didn't play ball.

47:21.174 --> 47:22.634
[Victor] What happened to 'em?

47:27.847 --> 47:28.973
To your brothers?

47:33.520 --> 47:34.688
The city took 'em.

47:36.815 --> 47:38.358
Just like it took your family.

47:41.361 --> 47:43.154
There was nothin' I could...

47:45.323 --> 47:46.700
I was, uh...

47:48.993 --> 47:49.994
too weak.

47:54.874 --> 47:57.585
My brothers and me, we used to
get into all kinds of trouble.

48:02.132 --> 48:04.217
Back then, when we was kids,

48:04.342 --> 48:06.011
we just had the city, you know?

48:07.220 --> 48:08.596
That was our playground.

48:21.985 --> 48:24.863
["A Forest" by The Cure playing]

48:29.868 --> 48:30.702
Hey, kid.

48:31.494 --> 48:32.579
Let's go.

48:32.704 --> 48:34.622
[helicopter whirring overhead]

48:34.622 --> 48:36.624
[Oz] You ever heard of
the underground trolleys?

48:36.624 --> 48:38.209
Used to run here.

48:38.335 --> 48:39.377
[Victor] No.

48:44.841 --> 48:45.884
[light buzzing]

48:49.095 --> 48:50.597
[barking]

48:52.390 --> 48:56.061
[dog continues barking]

49:01.066 --> 49:02.484
[metal clanging]

49:03.193 --> 49:04.319
[metal screeching]

49:10.533 --> 49:11.826
[metal chain snaps]

49:12.577 --> 49:15.121
[metal clanging]

49:18.625 --> 49:21.252
[hinge creaking]

49:25.882 --> 49:27.092
[Oz] Me and my brothers,

49:27.217 --> 49:28.968
we used to mess around
down here a lot.

49:29.719 --> 49:31.513
These tunnels,
they go everywhere.

49:32.764 --> 49:35.100
Gave us access to
the whole damn city.

49:36.226 --> 49:37.018
Come on.

49:37.018 --> 49:39.396
How long have these been here?

49:39.396 --> 49:41.064
[Oz] They were abandoned
when I was a kid.

49:41.064 --> 49:43.066
Politicians got greedy.

49:43.066 --> 49:44.401
Diverted funds.

49:44.401 --> 49:46.361
One day, the trolleys
just stopped runnin'.

49:47.821 --> 49:49.781
["A Forest" continues playing]

49:49.906 --> 49:51.825
[liquid dripping]

50:03.336 --> 50:04.546
[Oz] Wow...

50:05.922 --> 50:06.881
Long time.

50:12.137 --> 50:13.847
[Victor] Wow. Holy shit.

50:13.972 --> 50:15.515
Fuckin' unbelievable, right?

50:34.325 --> 50:38.371
[generator sputtering]

50:39.664 --> 50:41.374
[generator whirring]

50:43.209 --> 50:44.502
[laughing]

50:45.211 --> 50:46.087
Huh?

50:49.049 --> 50:50.300
[Victor] Whoa...

50:50.300 --> 50:52.385
[dramatic music playing]

50:56.681 --> 50:58.016
[Oz] It's gonna take some work,

50:58.141 --> 51:00.643
you know, to get it into shape,

51:00.643 --> 51:02.020
but once we do...

51:03.521 --> 51:04.564
Hey, kid!

51:05.315 --> 51:06.566
You feel that, right?

51:07.317 --> 51:09.235
It's humid down here, dark.

51:09.235 --> 51:11.363
You know what thrives
in a place like this?

51:12.405 --> 51:14.282
- Mushrooms?
- Bingo.

51:16.034 --> 51:17.619
Yeah, mushrooms.

51:19.245 --> 51:21.456
Welcome to our new
base of operations.

51:21.456 --> 51:22.874
[chuckles]

51:23.541 --> 51:24.751
This fuckin' place...

51:27.253 --> 51:28.546
callin' me home.

51:29.839 --> 51:31.841
[generator sputtering]

51:31.841 --> 51:34.427
[dramatic music swells]

51:34.427 --> 51:36.137
- [electricity crackles]
- [bulb explodes]

51:36.137 --> 51:38.932
[generator sputters, stops]

51:39.057 --> 51:41.976
["Reckless" by St. Vincent
playing]

51:48.525 --> 51:52.821
♪ And I've been
mourning you since ♪

51:52.821 --> 51:57.909
♪ The day I met you ♪

52:00.495 --> 52:02.497
♪ And a stranger come
in my path ♪

52:02.497 --> 52:05.333
♪ And I'll eat you up, I ♪

52:06.042 --> 52:08.211
♪ I tear you limb from limb ♪

52:08.211 --> 52:11.923
♪ Or I'll fall in love ♪

52:11.923 --> 52:17.762
♪ Reckless, reckless ♪

52:17.762 --> 52:21.433
♪ Reckless ♪

52:23.852 --> 52:26.730
♪ If your love was an anchor ♪

52:26.730 --> 52:29.733
♪ And I am lost at sea ♪

52:29.733 --> 52:32.944
♪ I hear the riders calling ♪

52:32.944 --> 52:37.157
♪ They're calling for me ♪

52:50.545 --> 52:52.464
♪ Calling for me ♪

52:53.506 --> 52:55.383
♪ Calling for me ♪

53:09.147 --> 53:12.734
[mysterious theme music playing]

54:01.157 --> 54:03.118
[music fades]
